# What tests/vt.sh's boot starts once the drivers are running: the
# demo's /etc/system with two terminals, which the demo itself does not
# start, so the test has them at known pids. The serial shell, which
# boot waits for; font, the font
# service; wm, the compositor; and two vts, pids 17 and 18, each a
# Terminal window with a tab, which the window's vt registers as vt1 or
# vt2, whichever is free first, on a port of its own, and whose shell,
# sh vt1 or sh vt2, it starts; a window closes when its last tab's shell
# exits.
# make vt-initramfs puts this over the demo's own.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/font
start /sbin/wm
start /Applications/Terminal.app/vt
start /Applications/Terminal.app/vt
